{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QuantumUniverses.QuantumUniverseExists","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QuantumUniverses.QuantumUniverseExists","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.CategoricalFoundations","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.TrivialWitness"],"declarations":1,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.exists_instance","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.exists_instance","kind":"theorem","line":22,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/quantum-universe-exists.lean#L22-L45","doc":"**Existence of a quantum universe over a commutative ring `R`.**\n\n**This was an `axiom` until 2026-08-16.**  The axiom's own docstring named\nthe witness — *\"a concrete witness (R-Mod or Rep(SU_q(2))) requires\ncategory/monoidal-category instances not yet provided\"* — and that turned\nout to be false: the instances are provided.  `ModuleCat R` with `A = 𝟙`\ndischarges every field, so the claim is now a theorem and the axiom is\nretired.\n\nBuilt in\n[`QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/TrivialWitness.lean`](../lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/TrivialWitness.lean);\n`#print axioms` reports only `propext`, `Classical.choice`, `Quot.sound`.\n\nNote the hypothesis weakened from `[Field k]` to `[CommRing R]` — the\nwitness never needed a field, matching `def:quantum-universe`, which asks\nfor an `R`-linear category over a commutative ring.\n\nThis does **not** extend to `QuantumObservableUniverse`: at `A = 𝟙` the\naugmentation ideal vanishes, so `adjoint_nontrivial` fails.  QOU existence\nstill rests on its own cited `sorry`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:quantum-universe-exists","label":"prop:quantum-universe-exists","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/quantum-universe-exists.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}